IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc14-part13-criminal-organization.l4 -- ss 467.1 to 467.2 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: criminal organization definitions and offences (in PART XIII).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Imports the keel's core (`ccc-core`).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text.
-- SEAMS: `s 467.1(1) the group is a criminal organization` and `s 467.1(1) the offence is a serious offence` are the answers the keel's `s 2 criminal organization` and `s 2 serious offence` take as inputs (PLAN.md section 6).
-- HOW A RESULT READS: JUST TRUE = the text brings the case within the provision; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered (see NOTES.md).

§ `ss 467.1 to 467.2 -- criminal organization offences`

§§ `s 467.1 -- Definitions ("The following definitions apply in this Act.")`

-- src:8478 | criminal organization means a group, however organized, that
-- src:8479 | (a) is composed of three or more persons in or outside Canada; and
-- src:8480 | (b) has as one of its main purposes or main activities the facilitation or commission of one or more serious offences that, if committed, would likely result in the direct or indirect receipt of a material benefit, including a financial benefit, by the group or by any of the persons who constitute the group.
-- src:8481 | It does not include a group of persons that forms randomly for the immediate commission of a single offence. (organisation criminelle)
@ref s 467.1(1) "criminal organization" (src:8478-8481)
GIVEN `a group, however organized` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons composing the group, in or outside Canada` IS A NUMBER
      `has as one of its main purposes or main activities the facilitation or commission of one or more offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those offences, if committed, would likely result in the direct or indirect receipt of a material benefit, including a financial benefit, by the group or by any of the persons who constitute the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offences are serious offences, by s 467.1(1) serious offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the group is a group of persons that forms randomly for the immediate commission of a single offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.1(1) the group is a criminal organization` MEANS
    IF NOT `a group, however organized`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "criminal organization means a group, however organized"
    ELSE IF `the number of persons composing the group, in or outside Canada` LESS THAN 3
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is composed of three or more persons in or outside Canada"
         ELSE IF `the group is a group of persons that forms randomly for the immediate commission of a single offence`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It does not include a group of persons that forms randomly for the immediate commission of a single offence"
              ELSE IF NOT `has as one of its main purposes or main activities the facilitation or commission of one or more offences`
                   THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has as one of its main purposes or main activities the facilitation or commission of one or more serious offences"
                   ELSE IF NOT `those offences, if committed, would likely result in the direct or indirect receipt of a material benefit, including a financial benefit, by the group or by any of the persons who constitute the group`
                        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "would likely result in the direct or indirect receipt of a material benefit, including a financial benefit"
                        ELSE `the offences are serious offences, by s 467.1(1) serious offence`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("means"); NOTHING when s 467.1(1) "serious offence" is itself not covered

-- src:8482 | serious offence means an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more, or another offence that is prescribed by regulation. (infraction grave)
@ref s 467.1(1) "serious offence" (src:8482)
GIVEN `the class of the offence` IS A `Class of offence`
      `the maximum imprisonment of the offence, its indictable limb or its only limb` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the offence is another offence that is prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.1(1) the offence is a serious offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is another offence that is prescribed by regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- "or another offence that is prescribed by regulation" (the regulations are outside the sources: the caller states whether the offence is prescribed)
    ELSE IF `the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "serious offence means an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament"
         ELSE CONSIDER `the maximum imprisonment of the offence, its indictable limb or its only limb`
              WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence section states no maximum punishment, so "imprisonment for five years or more" cannot be tested here
              WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` longest THEN
                  IF (longest's years TIMES 12 PLUS longest's months) AT LEAST 60 AND NOT (longest's `less a day` AND (longest's years TIMES 12 PLUS longest's months) EQUALS 60 AND longest's days EQUALS 0)
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for which the maximum punishment is imprisonment for five years or more"

-- src:8484 | (2) For the purposes of this section, section 467.11 and 467.111, facilitation of an offence does not require knowledge of a particular offence the commission of which is facilitated, or that an offence actually be committed.
@ref s 467.1(2) (src:8484)
GIVEN `the provision in question` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the requirement asked about is knowledge of a particular offence the commission of which is facilitated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement asked about is that an offence actually be committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.1(2) facilitation of an offence requires knowledge of a particular offence, or that an offence actually be committed` MEANS
    IF (`the provision in question`'s `section` EQUALS 467.1 OR `the provision in question`'s `section` EQUALS 467.11 OR `the provision in question`'s `section` EQUALS 467.111)
        AND (`the requirement asked about is knowledge of a particular offence the commission of which is facilitated` OR `the requirement asked about is that an offence actually be committed`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "facilitation of an offence does not require knowledge of a particular offence the commission of which is facilitated, or that an offence actually be committed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of this section, section 467.11 and 467.111"

-- src:8486 | (3) In this section and in sections 467.11 to 467.13, committing an offence means being a party to it or counselling any person to be a party to it.
@ref s 467.1(3) (src:8486)
GIVEN `the provision in question` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person counsels any person to be a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.1(3) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the provision in question`'s `section` EQUALS 467.1 OR (`the provision in question`'s `section` AT LEAST 467.11 AND `the provision in question`'s `section` AT MOST 467.13)
    THEN (IF `the person is a party to the offence` OR `the person counsels any person to be a party to the offence`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "committing an offence means being a party to it or counselling any person to be a party to it"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section and in sections 467.11 to 467.13"

-- src:8488 | (4) The Governor in Council may make regulations prescribing offences that are included in the definition serious offence in subsection (1).
@ref s 467.1(4) (src:8488)
`s 467.1(4) the regulation-making power, as the text shows it` MEANS "The Governor in Council may make regulations prescribing offences that are included in the definition serious offence in subsection (1)."

§§ `s 467.11 -- Participation in activities of criminal organization`

-- src:8490 | 467.11 (1) Every person who, for the purpose of enhancing the ability of a criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament, knowingly, by act or omission, participates in or contributes to any activity of the criminal organization is guilty of
-- src:8491 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:8492 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 467.11(1) (src:8490-8492)
GIVEN `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `for the purpose of enhancing the ability of the criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by act or omission, participates in or contributes to any activity of the criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.11(1) the person commits the offence of participating in the activities of a criminal organization` MEANS
    IF `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND `for the purpose of enhancing the ability of the criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament`
        AND `knowingly`
        AND `by act or omission, participates in or contributes to any activity of the criminal organization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the purpose of enhancing the ability of a criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament, knowingly, by act or omission, participates in or contributes to any activity of the criminal organization"

@ref s 467.11(1) (src:8490-8492)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 467.11(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 467.11(1) (src:8491-8492)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 467.11(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (a)
       , (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (b)

DECLARE `s 467.11(2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 467.11(2)(a) the criminal organization actually facilitated or committed an indictable offence`
    `s 467.11(2)(b) the participation or contribution of the accused actually enhanced the ability of the criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence`
    `s 467.11(2)(c) the accused knew the specific nature of any indictable offence that may have been facilitated or committed by the criminal organization`
    `s 467.11(2)(d) the accused knew the identity of any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization`
    `s 467.11(2) a matter that is none of those`

-- src:8494 | (2) In a prosecution for an offence under subsection (1), it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that
-- src:8495 | (a) the criminal organization actually facilitated or committed an indictable offence;
-- src:8496 | (b) the participation or contribution of the accused actually enhanced the ability of the criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence;
-- src:8497 | (c) the accused knew the specific nature of any indictable offence that may have been facilitated or committed by the criminal organization; or
-- src:8498 | (d) the accused knew the identity of any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization.
@ref s 467.11(2) (src:8494-8498)
GIVEN `the prosecution is for an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 467.11(2) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.11(2) it is necessary for the prosecutor to prove the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prosecution is for an offence under subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a prosecution for an offence under subsection (1)"
    ELSE CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `s 467.11(2) a matter that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that"
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that"

DECLARE `s 467.11(3) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 467.11(3)(a) uses a name, word, symbol or other representation that identifies, or is associated with, the criminal organization`
    `s 467.11(3)(b) frequently associates with any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization`
    `s 467.11(3)(c) receives any benefit from the criminal organization`
    `s 467.11(3)(d) repeatedly engages in activities at the instruction of any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization`
    `s 467.11(3) a factor that is none of those named`

-- src:8500 | (3) In determining whether an accused participates in or contributes to any activity of a criminal organization, the Court may consider, among other factors, whether the accused
-- src:8501 | (a) uses a name, word, symbol or other representation that identifies, or is associated with, the criminal organization;
-- src:8502 | (b) frequently associates with any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization;
-- src:8503 | (c) receives any benefit from the criminal organization; or
-- src:8504 | (d) repeatedly engages in activities at the instruction of any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization.
@ref s 467.11(3) (src:8500-8504)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 467.11(3) factor`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.11(3) the court may consider the factor in determining whether the accused participates in or contributes to an activity of a criminal organization` MEANS
    CONSIDER factor
    WHEN `s 467.11(3) a factor that is none of those named` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the Court may consider, among other factors"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 467.111 -- Recruitment of members by a criminal organization`

-- src:8506 | 467.111 Every person who, for the purpose of enhancing the ability of a criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament, recruits, solicits, encourages, coerces or invites a person to join the criminal organization, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable,
-- src:8507 | (a) in the case where the person recruited, solicited, encouraged or invited is under 18 years of age, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years, and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months; and
-- src:8508 | (b) in any other case, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years.
@ref s 467.111 (src:8506-8508)
GIVEN `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `for the purpose of enhancing the ability of the criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `recruits, solicits, encourages, coerces or invites a person to join the criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.111 the person commits the offence of recruiting members for a criminal organization` MEANS
    IF `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND `for the purpose of enhancing the ability of the criminal organization to facilitate or commit an indictable offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament`
        AND `recruits, solicits, encourages, coerces or invites a person to join the criminal organization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "recruits, solicits, encourages, coerces or invites a person to join the criminal organization"

@ref s 467.111 (src:8506)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 467.111 the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- (a) a person under 18: not exceeding five years, and a minimum punishment of imprisonment for six months; (b) any other case: not exceeding five years.
@ref s 467.111 (src:8507-8508)
GIVEN `the person recruited, solicited, encouraged or invited is under 18 years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 467.111 the punishment` MEANS
    IF `the person recruited, solicited, encouraged or invited is under 18 years of age`
    THEN LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (a)
    ELSE LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)   -- (b)

§§ `s 467.12 -- Commission of offence for criminal organization`

-- src:8510 | 467.12 (1) Every person who commits an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years.
@ref s 467.12(1) (src:8510)
GIVEN `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person commits an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament, by s 467.1(3) the person commits the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, the criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.12(1) the person commits the offence of committing an offence for a criminal organization` MEANS
    IF `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND `the person commits an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament, by s 467.1(3) the person commits the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND `for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, the criminal organization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commits an indictable offence under this or any other Act of Parliament for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, a criminal organization"

@ref s 467.12(1) (src:8510)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 467.12(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 467.12(1) (src:8510)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 467.12(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

-- src:8512 | (2) In a prosecution for an offence under subsection (1), it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that the accused knew the identity of any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization.
@ref s 467.12(2) (src:8512)
GIVEN `the prosecution is for an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.12(2) it is necessary for the prosecutor to prove that the accused knew the identity of any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization` MEANS
    IF `the prosecution is for an offence under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that the accused knew the identity of any of the persons who constitute the criminal organization"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a prosecution for an offence under subsection (1)"

§§ `s 467.13 -- Instructing commission of offence for criminal organization`

-- src:8514 | 467.13 (1) Every person who is one of the persons who constitute a criminal organization and who knowingly instructs, directly or indirectly, any person to commit an offence under this or any other Act of Parliament for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, the criminal organization is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life.
@ref s 467.13(1) (src:8514)
GIVEN `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is one of the persons who constitute the criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `knowingly instructs, directly or indirectly, any person to commit an offence under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, the criminal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.13(1) the person commits the offence of instructing the commission of an offence for a criminal organization` MEANS
    IF `the group is a criminal organization, by s 467.1(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND `the person is one of the persons who constitute the criminal organization`
        AND `knowingly instructs, directly or indirectly, any person to commit an offence under this or any other Act of Parliament`
        AND `for the benefit of, at the direction of, or in association with, the criminal organization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is one of the persons who constitute a criminal organization and who knowingly instructs, directly or indirectly, any person to commit an offence"

@ref s 467.13(1) (src:8514)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 467.13(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 467.13(1) (src:8514)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 467.13(1) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)

DECLARE `s 467.13(2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 467.13(2)(a) an offence other than the offence under subsection (1) was actually committed`
    `s 467.13(2)(b) the accused instructed a particular person to commit an offence`
    `s 467.13(2)(c) the accused knew the identity of all of the persons who constitute the criminal organization`
    `s 467.13(2) a matter that is none of those`

-- src:8516 | (2) In a prosecution for an offence under subsection (1), it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that
-- src:8517 | (a) an offence other than the offence under subsection (1) was actually committed;
-- src:8518 | (b) the accused instructed a particular person to commit an offence; or
