@ref s 467.13(2) (src:8516-8519)
GIVEN `the prosecution is for an offence under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 467.13(2) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.13(2) it is necessary for the prosecutor to prove the matter` MEANS
    IF NOT `the prosecution is for an offence under subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a prosecution for an offence under subsection (1)"
    ELSE CONSIDER matter
         WHEN `s 467.13(2) a matter that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that"
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is not necessary for the prosecutor to prove that"

§§ `s 467.14 -- Sentences to be served consecutively`

-- src:8521 | 467.14 A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under section 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13 shall be served consecutively to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events and to any other sentence to which the person is subject at the time the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under any of those sections.
@ref s 467.14 (src:8521)
GIVEN `the provision the sentence is imposed under` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `another punishment was imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to another sentence at the time the sentence is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 467.14 the sentence is to be served consecutively to the other punishment or sentence` MEANS
    IF (`the provision the sentence is imposed under`'s `section` EQUALS 467.11 OR `the provision the sentence is imposed under`'s `section` EQUALS 467.111
            OR `the provision the sentence is imposed under`'s `section` EQUALS 467.12 OR `the provision the sentence is imposed under`'s `section` EQUALS 467.13)
        AND (`another punishment was imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` OR `the person is subject to another sentence at the time the sentence is imposed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under section 467.11, 467.111, 467.12 or 467.13 shall be served consecutively"

